+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`: it
+returns the value the pointer refers to, and throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer or does
+not resolve to a value of the document. Later features build on it.
+
+# Behaviour
+
+- `""` refers to the whole document; otherwise the pointer must start with `/`.
+- `~1` decodes to `/`, `~0` to `~` (in that order); any other `~` escape is invalid.
+- Objects: own properties only (no prototype lookups). Arrays: token must be `0` or a non-zero-leading
+  decimal index within bounds; `-` (past the end) and leading zeros do not resolve.
+- Primitives and `null` have no children.
